INSERT INTO `tabOnboarding Step` VALUES ('Accounts Settings','2021-06-29 16:42:03.400731','2021-08-13 11:50:06.227835','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Accounts Settings',0,0,'# Account Settings\n\nIn ERPNext, Accounting features are configurable as per your business needs. Accounts Settings is the place to define some of your accounting preferences like:\n\n - Credit Limit and over billing settings\n - Taxation preferences\n - Deferred accounting preferences\n',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Take a quick walk-through of Accounts Settings','Accounts Settings',0,0,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Add Blog Category','2020-04-28 22:08:38.555550','2020-05-28 13:51:53.157256','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Add Blog Category',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Blog Category',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Asset Category','2021-08-13 14:26:18.656303','2021-11-23 10:02:03.242127','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Define Asset Category',0,0,'# Asset Category\n\nAn Asset Category classifies different assets of a Company.\n\nYou can create an Asset Category based on the type of assets. For example, all your desktops and laptops can be part of an Asset Category named \"Electronic Equipments\". Create a separate category for furniture. Also, you can update default properties for each category, like:\n - Depreciation type and duration\n - Fixed asset account\n - Depreciation account\n',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Let\'s review existing Asset Category','Asset Category',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Asset Item','2021-08-13 14:27:07.277167','2021-12-02 11:23:48.158504','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create an Asset Item',0,0,'# Asset Item\n\nAsset items are created based on Asset Category. You can create one or multiple items against once Asset Category. The sales and purchase transaction for Asset is done via Asset Item. ',NULL,'Create Entry','Let\'s create a new Asset item','Item',1,1,'Item',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Asset Purchase','2021-08-13 14:27:53.678621','2021-11-23 10:02:03.235498','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Purchase an Asset',0,0,'# Purchase an Asset\n\nAssets purchases process if done following the standard Purchase cycle. If capital work in progress is enabled in Asset Category, Asset will be created as soon as Purchase Receipt is created for it. You can quickly create a Purchase Receipt for Asset and see its impact on books of accounts.',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Let\'s create a Purchase Receipt','Purchase Receipt',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Buying Settings','2020-05-06 15:53:44.667414','2020-05-12 18:30:06.323797','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Configure Buying Settings.',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Update Settings',NULL,'Buying Settings',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Chart of Accounts','2020-05-13 19:58:20.928127','2022-06-07 14:21:26.264769','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Review Chart of Accounts',0,0,'# Chart Of Accounts\n\nERPNext sets up a simple chart of accounts for each Company you create, but you can modify it according to business and legal requirements.','https://www.youtube.com/embed/AcfMCT7wLLo','Go to Page','Learn more about Chart of Accounts','Account',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tree/Account','Explore Chart of Accounts','You can continue with the onboarding after exploring this page',0,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/embed/AcfMCT7wLLo',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Check Stock Ledger Report','2023-05-29 13:46:04.174565','2023-05-29 14:39:03.943244','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Check Stock Ledger',0,0,'# Check Stock Reports\nBased on the various stock transactions, you can get a host of one-click Stock Reports in ERPNext like Stock Ledger, Stock Balance, Projected Quantity, and Ageing analysis.',NULL,'View Report','Check Stock Ledger',NULL,0,0,NULL,0,'Stock Ledger','Stock Ledger Entry','Script Report','Stock Ledger report contains every submitted stock transaction. You can use filter to narrow down ledger entries.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Company Set Up','2021-11-22 11:55:48.931427','2023-05-15 09:18:42.895537','Administrator','Administrator',0,1,'Set Up a Company',0,0,'# Set Up a Company\n\nA company is a legal entity for which you will set up your books of account and create accounting transactions. In ERPNext, you can create multiple companies, and establish relationships (group/subsidiary) among them.\n\nWithin the company master, you can capture various default accounts for that Company and set crucial settings related to the accounting methodology followed for a company.\n',NULL,'Create Entry','Let\'s review your Company','Company',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Configure Account Settings','2020-05-14 17:53:00.876946','2020-10-19 14:40:55.584484','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Configure Account Settings',0,0,'# Account Settings\n\nThis is a crucial piece of configuration. There are various account settings in ERPNext to restrict and configure actions in the Accounting module.\n\nThe following settings are avaialble for you to configure\n\n1. Account Freezing \n2. Credit and Overbilling\n3. Invoicing and Tax Automations\n4. Balance Sheet configurations\n\nThere\'s much more, you can check it all out in this step',NULL,'Show Form Tour',NULL,'Accounts Settings',1,0,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Cost Centers for Report and Budgeting','2021-07-12 12:02:05.726608','2021-08-13 11:55:08.510366','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Cost Centers for Budgeting and Analysis',0,0,'# Cost Centers for Budgeting and Analysis\n\nWhile your Books of Accounts are framed to fulfill statutory requirements, you can set up Cost Center and Accounting Dimensions to address your companies reporting and budgeting requirements.\n\nClick here to learn more about how  <b>[Cost Center](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/cost-center)</b> and <b> [Dimensions](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/accounting-dimensions)</b> allow you to get advanced financial analytics reports from ERPNext.',NULL,'Go to Page','View Cost Center Tree',NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cost-center/view/tree',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Customer','2020-05-14 17:46:41.831517','2023-05-23 12:45:55.138580','Administrator','Administrator',0,1,'Create a Customer',0,0,'# Create a Customer\n\nThe Customer master is at the heart of your sales transactions. Customers are linked in Quotations, Sales Orders, Invoices, and Payments. Customers can be either numbered or identified by name (you would typically do this based on the number of customers you have).\n\nThrough Customer’s master, you can effectively track essentials like:\n - Customer’s multiple address and contacts\n - Account Receivables\n - Credit Limit and Credit Period\n',NULL,'Create Entry','Let’s create your first Customer','Customer',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Fixed Asset Item','2020-05-08 13:20:00.259985','2020-05-08 13:20:00.259985','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create a Fixed Asset Item',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Item',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Material Request','2020-05-15 14:39:09.818764','2021-08-24 18:08:08.347501','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Track Material Request',0,0,'# Track Material Request\n\n\nAlso known as Purchase Request or an Indent, is a document identifying a requirement of a set of items (products or services) for various purposes like procurement, transfer, issue, or manufacturing. Once the Material Request is validated, a purchase manager can take the next actions for purchasing items like requesting RFQ from a supplier or directly placing an order with an identified Supplier.\n\n',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Let’s create your first Material Request','Material Request',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Product','2020-05-12 18:16:06.624554','2020-10-30 15:20:30.133495','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create a Sales Item',0,0,'## Products and Services\n\nDepending on the nature of your business, you might be selling products or services to your clients or even both. \nERPNext is optimized for itemized management of your sales and purchase.\n\nThe **Item Master**  is where you can add all your sales items. If you are in services, you can create an Item for each service that you offer. If you run a manufacturing business, the same master is used for keeping a record of raw materials, sub-assemblies etc.\n\nCompleting the Item Master is very essential for the successful implementation of ERPNext. We have a brief video introducing the item master for you, you can watch it in the next step.','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sl5UFA5H5EQ','Create Entry',NULL,'Item',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Quotation','2020-06-01 13:34:58.958641','2023-05-15 09:18:42.984170','Administrator','Administrator',0,1,'Create your first Quotation',0,0,'# Create a Quotation\n\nLet’s get started with business transactions by creating your first Quotation. You can create a Quotation for an existing customer or a prospect. It will be an approved document, with items you sell and the proposed price + taxes applied. After completing the instructions, you will get a Quotation in a ready to share print format.',NULL,'Create Entry','Let’s create your first Quotation','Quotation',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Sales Order','2021-06-29 21:22:54.204880','2021-06-29 21:22:54.204880','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create a Sales Order',0,0,'A Sales Order is a confirmation of an order from your customer. It is also referred to as Proforma Invoice.\n\nSales Order at the heart of your sales and purchase transactions. Sales Orders are linked in Delivery Note, Sales Invoices, Material Request, and Maintenance transactions. Through Sales Order, you can track fulfillment of the overall deal towards the customer.',NULL,'Create Entry','Create Sales Order','Sales Order',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Stock Entry','2020-05-15 03:20:16.277043','2023-05-29 14:39:04.066547','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Manage Stock Movements',0,0,'# Manage Stock Movements\nStock entry allows you to register the movement of stock for various purposes like transfer, received, issues, repacked, etc. To address issues related to theft and pilferages,  you can always ensure that the movement of goods happens against a document reference Stock Entry in ERPNext.\n\nLet’s get a quick walk-through on the various scenarios covered in Stock Entry by watching [*this video*](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Njt107hlY3I).',NULL,'Create Entry','Create a Material Transfer Entry','Stock Entry',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Supplier','2020-05-14 22:09:10.043554','2023-05-19 15:32:55.069257','Administrator','Administrator',0,1,'Create a Supplier',0,0,'# Create a Supplier\n\nAlso known as Vendor, is a master at the center of your purchase transactions. Suppliers are linked in Request for Quotation, Purchase Orders, Receipts, and Payments. Suppliers can be either numbered or identified by name.\n\nThrough Supplier’s master, you can effectively track essentials like:\n - Supplier’s multiple address and contacts\n - Account Receivables\n - Credit Limit and Credit Period\n',NULL,'Create Entry','Let’s create your first Supplier','Supplier',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create a Warehouse','2021-05-17 16:13:19.297789','2023-05-29 14:39:04.074907','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Setup a Warehouse',0,0,'# Setup a Warehouse\nThe warehouse can be your location/godown/store where you maintain the item\'s inventory, and receive/deliver them to various parties.\n\nIn ERPNext, you can maintain a Warehouse in the tree structure, so that location and sub-location of an item can be tracked. Also, you can link a Warehouse to a specific Accounting ledger, where the real-time stock value of that warehouse’s item will be reflected.',NULL,'Create Entry','Let’s create your first  warehouse ','Warehouse',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create an Asset','2020-05-08 13:21:53.332538','2020-05-08 13:21:53.332538','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create an Asset',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Asset',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create an Asset Category','2020-05-08 13:21:53.332538','2020-05-08 13:21:53.332538','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create an Asset Category',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Asset Category',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create an Item','2021-05-17 13:47:18.515052','2023-05-23 12:43:08.484206','Administrator','Administrator',0,1,'Create an Item',0,0,'# Create an Item\n\nItem is a product or a service offered by your company, or something you buy as a part of your supplies or raw materials.\n\nItems are integral to everything you do in ERPNext - from billing, purchasing to managing inventory. Everything you buy or sell, whether it is a physical product or a service is an Item. Items can be stock, non-stock, variants, serialized, batched, assets, etc.\n','','Create Entry','Create a new Item','Item',0,1,'Item General',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create and Send Quotation','2020-05-09 23:42:46.592075','2020-05-28 21:07:11.461172','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create and Send Quotation',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Quotation',1,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create Blogger','2020-04-28 22:08:20.907705','2020-04-30 19:06:10.694419','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create Blogger',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Blogger',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create BOM','2020-05-05 16:41:20.239696','2021-08-13 16:00:51.092671','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Bill of Materials',0,0,'# Create a Bill of Materials\n\nA Bill of Materials (BOM) is a list of items and sub-assemblies with quantities required to manufacture an Item.\n\nBOM also provides cost estimation for the production of the item. It takes raw-materials cost based on valuation and operations to cost based on routing, which gives total costing for a BOM.',NULL,'Create Entry','Create your first Bill of Materials','BOM',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create Lead','2020-05-09 23:40:25.192503','2020-05-28 21:07:01.373403','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create Lead',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Lead',1,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create Opportunity','2020-05-14 17:38:27.496696','2021-01-21 15:28:52.483839','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create Opportunity',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Opportunity',1,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create Product','2020-05-05 16:42:31.476275','2021-08-13 16:00:22.407811','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Finished Items',0,0,'# Create Items for Bill of Materials\n\nOne of the prerequisites of a BOM is the creation of raw materials, sub-assembly, and finished items. Once these items are created, you will be able to proceed to the Bill of Materials master, which is composed of items and routing.\n',NULL,'Create Entry','Create an Item','Item',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create Raw Materials','2020-05-19 11:53:17.295372','2020-05-19 11:53:25.147837','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create Raw Materials',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Item',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create Your First Purchase Invoice','2020-05-14 22:10:07.049704','2021-08-13 11:56:11.677253','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create Your First Purchase Invoice ',0,0,'# Create your first Purchase Invoice\n\nA Purchase Invoice is a bill received from a Supplier for a product(s) or service(s) delivery to your company. You can track payables through Purchase Invoice and process Payment Entries against it.\n\nPurchase Invoices can also be created against a Purchase Order or Purchase Receipt.',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Let’s create your first Purchase Invoice','Purchase Invoice',1,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create your first Purchase Order','2020-05-12 18:17:49.976035','2021-08-24 18:08:08.936484','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create first Purchase Order',0,0,'# Create first Purchase Order\n\nPurchase Order is at the heart of your buying transactions. In ERPNext, Purchase Order can can be created against a Purchase Material Request (indent) and Supplier Quotation as well.  Purchase Orders is also linked to Purchase Receipt and Purchase Invoices, allowing you to keep a birds-eye view on your purchase deals.\n\n',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Let’s create your first Purchase Order','Purchase Order',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create Your First Sales Invoice','2020-05-14 17:48:21.019019','2023-05-22 21:20:15.589644','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create Your First Sales Invoice ',0,0,'# All about sales invoice\n\nA Sales Invoice is a bill that you send to your Customers against which the Customer makes the payment. Sales Invoice is an accounting transaction. On submission of Sales Invoice, the system updates the receivable and books income against a Customer Account.',NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Sales Invoice',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Create your first Sales Order','2020-06-01 12:52:27.181841','2020-06-01 12:52:27.181841','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create your first Sales Order',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Sales Order',1,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('CRM Settings','2022-01-29 20:14:24.803844','2022-01-29 20:14:24.803844','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'CRM Settings',0,0,'# CRM Settings\n\nCRM module’s features are configurable as per your business needs. CRM Settings is the place where you can set your preferences for:\n- Campaign\n- Lead\n- Opportunity\n- Quotation',NULL,'Go to Page',NULL,'CRM Settings',0,0,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'#crm-settings/CRM%20Settings',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Custom Doctype','2021-11-23 12:30:04.407568','2021-11-23 12:30:04.407568','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Custom Document Types',0,0,'A DocType (Document Type) is used to insert forms in ERPNext. Forms such as Customer, Orders, and Invoices are Doctypes in the backend. You can also create new DocTypes to create new forms in ERPNext as per your business needs.',NULL,'Create Entry','Learn more about creating new DocTypes','DocType',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Custom Field','2021-11-23 12:21:09.479808','2021-11-23 12:21:09.479808','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create Custom Fields',0,0,'Every form in ERPNext has a standard set of fields. If you need to capture some information, but there is no standard Field available for it, you can insert Custom Field for it.\n\nOnce custom fields are added, you can use them for reports and analytics charts as well.\n',NULL,'Create Entry','Learn how to add Custom Fields','Custom Field',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Data import','2021-05-19 05:29:16.809610','2023-05-15 09:18:42.962231','Administrator','Administrator',0,1,'Import Data from Spreadsheet',0,0,'# Import Data from Spreadsheet\n\nIn ERPNext, you can easily migrate your historical data using spreadsheets. You can use it for migrating not just masters (like Customer, Supplier, Items), but also for transactions like (outstanding invoices, opening stock and accounting entries, etc).',NULL,'Watch Video','Learn more about data migration',NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://youtu.be/DQyqeurPI64',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Enable Website Tracking','2020-04-28 22:09:12.089238','2020-04-30 20:22:50.778590','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Enable Website Tracking',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Update Settings',NULL,'Website Settings',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,'enable_view_tracking','1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Existing Asset','2021-08-13 14:28:30.650459','2021-08-16 14:03:48.850471','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Add an Existing Asset',0,0,'# Add an Existing Asset\n\nIf you are just starting with ERPNext, you will need to enter Assets you already possess. You can add them as existing fixed assets in ERPNext. Please note that you will have to make a Journal Entry separately updating the opening balance in the fixed asset account.',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Add an existing Asset','Asset',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Explore Manufacturing Settings','2020-05-19 11:55:11.378374','2021-08-13 15:59:32.145655','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Manufacturing Settings',0,0,'# Review Manufacturing Settings\n\nIn ERPNext, the Manufacturing module’s features are configurable as per your business needs. Manufacturing Settings is the place where you can set your preferences for:\n\n- Capacity planning for allocating jobs to workstations\n- Raw-material consumption based on BOM or actual\n- Default values and over-production allowance\n',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Take a walk-through of Manufacturing Settings','Manufacturing Settings',0,0,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UVGfzwOOZC4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Financial Statements','2021-07-12 12:08:47.026115','2021-08-13 11:59:18.767407','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Financial Statements',0,0,'# Financial Statements\n\nIn ERPNext, you can get crucial financial reports like [Balance Sheet] and [Profit and Loss] statements with a click of a button. You can run in the report for a different period and plot analytics charts premised on statement data. For more reports, check sections like Financial Statements, General Ledger, and Profitability reports.\n\n<b>[Check Accounting reports](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/accounting-reports)</b>',NULL,'View Report',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,'General Ledger','GL Entry','Script Report','General Ledger',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Fixed Asset Accounts','2021-08-13 14:23:09.297765','2021-11-23 10:02:03.229566','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Review Fixed Asset Accounts',0,0,'# Fixed Asset Accounts\n\nWith the company, a host of fixed asset accounts are pre-configured. To ensure your asset transactions are leading to correct accounting entries, you can review and set up following asset accounts as per your business  requirements.\n - Fixed asset accounts (Asset account)\n - Accumulated depreciation\n - Capital Work in progress (CWIP) account\n - Asset Depreciation account (Expense account)',NULL,'Go to Page','Let\'s walk-through Chart of Accounts to review setup',NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'app/account/view/tree',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Introduction to Assets','2020-05-08 13:18:25.424715','2020-05-08 16:06:16.625646','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Introduction to Assets',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Watch Video',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I-K8pLRmvSo',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Introduction to Buying','2020-05-06 15:37:09.477765','2021-08-24 18:08:08.345735','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Buying Settings',0,0,'# Buying Settings\n\n\nBuying module’s features are highly configurable as per your business needs. Buying Settings is the place where you can set your preferences for:\n\n- Supplier naming and default values\n- Billing and shipping preference in buying transactions\n\n\n',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Let’s walk-through few Buying Settings','Buying Settings',1,1,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://youtu.be/efFajTTQBa8',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Introduction to CRM','2020-05-09 23:37:08.926812','2020-05-14 17:28:16.448676','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Introduction to CRM',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Watch Video',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o9XCSZHJfpA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Introduction to Manufacturing','2020-05-05 16:40:23.676406','2020-05-14 19:11:57.152883','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Manufacturing Settings',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Update Settings',NULL,'Manufacturing Settings',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UVGfzwOOZC4',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Introduction to Selling','2020-06-01 12:44:32.089234','2020-06-01 13:29:13.703177','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Introduction to Selling',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Watch Video',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://youtu.be/1eP90MWoDQM',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Introduction to Stock Entry','2020-05-15 02:47:17.958806','2021-05-18 15:13:43.306064','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Introduction to Stock Entry',0,0,'# Introduction to Stock Entry\nThis video will give a quick introduction to [**Stock Entry**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/stock-entry).',NULL,'Watch Video',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Njt107hlY3I',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Introduction to Website','2020-04-28 22:09:02.120939','2020-05-28 13:51:51.485924','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Introduction to Website',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Watch Video',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lyW6mfFBSNw',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Letterhead','2021-11-22 12:36:34.583783','2023-05-15 09:18:42.995184','Administrator','Administrator',0,1,'Setup Your Letterhead',0,0,'# Create a Letter Head\n\nA Letter Head contains your organization\'s name, logo, address, etc which appears at the header and footer portion in documents. You can learn more about Setting up Letter Head in ERPNext here.\n',NULL,'Create Entry','Let’s setup your first Letter Head','Letter Head',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Naming Series','2021-11-23 13:57:45.091427','2021-11-24 15:04:14.662684','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Setup Naming Series',0,0,'Each document created in ERPNext can have a unique ID generated for it, using a prefix defined for it. Though each document has some prefix pre-configured, you can further customize it using tools like Naming Series Tool and Document Naming Rule.\n',NULL,'Watch Video',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://youtu.be/IGyISSfI1qU',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Navigation Help','2021-11-22 12:09:52.233872','2023-05-16 12:53:25.939908','Administrator','Administrator',0,1,'How to Navigate in ERPNext',0,0,'# Navigation in ERPNext\n\nEase of navigating and browsing around the ERPNext is one of our core strengths. In the following video, you will learn how to reach a specific feature in ERPNext via module page or AwesomeBar.',NULL,'Watch Video','Learn about  Navigation options',NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://youtu.be/j60xyNFqX_A',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Operation','2020-05-12 16:15:31.706756','2021-08-13 15:59:53.313532','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Operation',0,0,'# Create Operations\n\nAn Operation refers to any manufacturing operation performed on the raw materials to process it further in the manufacturing path. As an example, if you are into garments manufacturing, you will create Operations like fabric cutting, stitching, and washing as some of the operations.',NULL,'Create Entry','Let’s create an Operation','Operation',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Print Format','2021-11-23 15:04:12.728513','2021-11-23 15:04:12.728513','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Customize Print Formats',0,0,'Print Formats allow you can define looks for documents when printed or converted to PDF. You can also create a custom Print Format using drag-and-drop tools.',NULL,'Create Entry','Learn about Standard and Custom Print Formats','Print Format',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Production Planning','2021-08-04 17:33:06.551077','2021-08-13 16:04:15.491414','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Production Planning',0,0,'# How Production Planning Works\n\nProduction Plan helps in production and material planning for the Items planned for manufacturing. These production items can be committed via Sales Order (to Customers) or Material Requests (internally).\n',NULL,'Create Entry','Learn more about Production Planning','Production Plan',1,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Purchase an Asset Item','2020-05-08 13:21:28.208059','2020-05-08 13:21:28.208059','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Purchase an Asset Item',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Purchase Receipt',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Report Builder','2021-11-24 17:04:18.762838','2021-11-24 17:04:18.762838','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Generate Custom Reports',0,0,'In each module, you will find a host of single-click reports, ranging from financial statements to sales and purchase analytics and stock tracking reports. If a required new report is not available out-of-the-box, you can create custom reports in ERPNext by pulling values from the same multiple ERPNext tables.\n',NULL,'Watch Video','Learn more about Report Builders','Report',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://youtu.be/TxJGUNarcQs',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Role Permissions','2021-11-23 14:00:27.208500','2021-11-24 15:04:14.615232','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Setup Limited Access for a User',0,0,'In ERPNext, you can add your Employees as Users, and give them restricted access. Tools like Role Permission and User Permission allow you to define rules which give restricted access to the user to masters and transactions.',NULL,'Watch Video',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://youtu.be/g3mk45o1zAg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Routing','2021-08-04 11:56:42.455758','2021-08-13 16:00:07.391563','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Routing',0,0,'# Setup Routing\n\nA Routing stores all Operations along with the description, hourly rate, operation time, batch size, etc. Click below to learn how the Routing template can be created, for quick selection in the BOM.',NULL,'Create Entry','Check help to setup Routing','Routing',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Sales Order','2021-08-13 14:03:49.217866','2021-08-24 18:12:32.394992','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Sales Order',0,0,'# Sales Order\n\nA Sales Order is a confirmation of an order from your customer. It is also referred to as Proforma Invoice.\n\nSales Order at the heart of your sales and purchase transactions. Sales Orders are linked in Delivery Note, Sales Invoices, Material Request, and Maintenance transactions. Through Sales Order, you can track fulfillment of the overall deal towards the customer.',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Let’s convert your first Sales Order against a Quotation','Sales Order',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Selling Settings','2020-06-01 13:01:45.615189','2021-08-24 18:11:21.264335','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Selling Settings',0,0,'# Selling Settings\n\nCRM and Selling module’s features are configurable as per your business needs. Selling Settings is the place where you can set your preferences for:\n - Customer naming and default values\n - Billing and shipping preference in sales transactions\n',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Let’s walk-through Selling Settings','Selling Settings',0,0,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Setup Taxes','2020-05-13 19:29:43.844463','2022-06-14 17:37:56.694261','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Setting up Taxes',0,0,'# Setting up Taxes\n\nERPNext lets you configure your taxes so that they are automatically applied in your buying and selling transactions. You can configure them globally or even on Items. ERPNext taxes are pre-configured for most regions.',NULL,'Create Entry','Manage Sales Tax Templates','Sales Taxes and Charges Template',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Setup your Warehouse','2020-05-19 18:54:19.383397','2021-05-17 13:53:06.936579','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Set up your Warehouse',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Go to Page',NULL,'Warehouse',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tree/Warehouse',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Stock Opening Balance','2021-05-17 16:13:47.511883','2023-05-29 14:39:08.825699','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Update Stock Opening Balance',0,0,'# Update Stock Opening Balance\nIt’s an entry to update the stock balance of an item, in a warehouse, on a date and time you are going live on ERPNext.\n\nOnce opening stocks are updated, you can create transactions like manufacturing and stock deliveries, where this opening stock will be consumed.',NULL,'Create Entry','Let’s create a stock opening entry','Stock Reconciliation',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nlHX0ZZ84Lw',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Stock Settings','2020-05-15 02:53:57.209967','2023-05-29 14:39:04.083360','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Review Stock Settings',0,0,'# Review Stock Settings\n\nIn ERPNext, the Stock module’s features are configurable as per your business needs. Stock Settings is the place where you can set your preferences for:\n- Default values for Item and Pricing\n- Default valuation method for inventory valuation\n- Set preference for serialization and batching of item\n- Set tolerance for over-receipt and delivery of items',NULL,'Show Form Tour','Take a walk through Stock Settings','Stock Settings',0,0,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Updating Opening Balances','2021-07-12 11:53:50.525030','2021-08-13 11:56:45.483418','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Updating Opening Balances',0,0,'# Updating Opening Balances\n\nOnce you close the financial statement in previous accounting software, you can update the same as opening in your ERPNext\'s Balance Sheet accounts. This will allow you to get complete financial statements from ERPNext in the coming years, and discontinue the parallel accounting system right away.','https://www.youtube.com/embed/U5wPIvEn-0c','Watch Video','Learn how to update opening balances',NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://www.youtube.com/embed/U5wPIvEn-0c',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('View Stock Projected Qty','2021-08-20 14:38:41.649103','2021-08-20 14:38:41.649103','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Check Stock Projected Qty',0,0,'# Check Stock Reports\nBased on the various stock transactions, you can get a host of one-click Stock Reports in ERPNext like Stock Ledger, Stock Balance, Projected Quantity, and Ageing analysis.',NULL,'View Report','Check Stock Projected Qty',NULL,0,0,NULL,0,'Stock Projected Qty','Item','Script Report','You can set the filters to narrow the results, then click on Generate New Report to see the updated report.',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('View Warehouses','2021-05-17 16:12:43.427579','2021-05-18 15:04:41.198413','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'View Warehouses',0,0,'# View Warehouse\nIn ERPNext the term \'warehouse\' can be thought of as a storage location.\n\nWarehouses are arranged in ERPNext in a tree like structure, where multiple sub-warehouses can be grouped under a single warehouse.\n\nIn this step we will view the [**Warehouse Tree**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/warehouse#21-tree-view) to view the [**Warehouses**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/warehouse) that are set by default.',NULL,'Go to Page',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tree/Warehouse',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Warehouse','2020-05-12 16:13:34.014554','2020-05-19 12:50:13.766712','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Create a Warehouse',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Create Entry',NULL,'Warehouse',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Web Page Tour','2020-05-13 12:32:15.966570','2020-05-28 13:51:54.264456','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Learn about Web Pages',0,0,NULL,NULL,'Show Form Tour',NULL,'Web Page',0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Work Order','2020-05-12 16:15:56.084682','2021-08-13 16:02:04.223536','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Work Order',0,0,'# Create a Work Order\n\nA Work Order or a Job order is given to the manufacturing shop floor by the Production Manager to initiate the manufacturing of a certain quantity of an item. Work Order carriers details of production Item, its BOM, quantities to be manufactured, and operations.\n\nThrough Work Order, you can track various production status like:\n\n- Issue of raw-material to shop material\n- Progress on each Workstation via Job Card\n- Manufactured Quantity against Work Order\n',NULL,'Create Entry','Create your first Work Order','Work Order',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Workflows','2021-11-23 13:58:58.530044','2021-11-24 15:04:14.632144','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Setup Approval Workflows',0,0,'Workflows allow you to define custom rules for the approval process of a particular document in ERPNext. You can also set complex Workflow Rules and set approval conditions.',NULL,'Watch Video',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,'https://youtu.be/yObJUg9FxFs',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),('Workstation','2020-05-12 16:14:14.930214','2021-08-13 15:59:59.634802','Administrator','Administrator',0,0,'Workstation',0,0,'# Create Workstations\n\nA Workstation stores information regarding the place where the workstation operations are performed. As an example, if you have ten sewing machines doing stitching jobs, each machine will be added as a workstation.',NULL,'Create Entry','Let’s create a Workstation','Workstation',1,1,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
